// Snippet: Commands
// Pattern: prying open a treasure chest — trigger host-side events
// Features: <<command>> dispatch with arguments, line tags (#dramatic, #sfx),
//            node tags, tagged lines
// Run: cargo run -p bubbles-tui -- examples/snippets/commands.bub
//
// Note: commands like <<play_fanfare>> and <<unlock_chest>> are emitted as
// DialogueEvent::Command events. In a real game your engine handles them
// (play audio, spawn particles, unlock doors, etc.). The TUI runner shows
// them in the transcript pane as "command_name args".

title: Start
tags: scene dungeon
---
You discover a barnacle-crusted chest half-buried in the sand. #atmospheric

-> Try the lid.
    <<creak_sound "chest_lid">>
    The lid grinds open with a sound like a drowning accordion. #sfx
    <<jump ContentsRevealed>>
-> Leave it alone.
    You: Last time you opened a chest it bit you. Not making that mistake again.
===

title: ContentsRevealed
---
Gold coins spill across the sand, glittering in the torchlight. #dramatic
<<play_fanfare "treasure_found">>
<<spawn_particles "gold_coins" 50>>

You: There must be three hundred doubloons here!
Ghostly Voice: That treasure is CURSED, ye fool! #eerie
<<play_sound "ghost_moan" 0.8>>

-> Take the gold anyway.
    <<give_gold 300>>
    <<apply_curse "greedy_pirate">>
    You: Worth it.
-> Back away slowly.
    You: On reflection, "cursed" is a dealbreaker.
===
